 Restore component, style, variable and prototype relationships in the received file. If you use Code Connect, verify the mapped component and code against the source library. Professional plans expose the active library and framework. Desktop uses the Dev Mode selection. Remote clients can request the framework label. [Code Connect and MCP](https://help.figma.com/hc/en-us/articles/42495296821911-Code-Connect-and-MCP).
 
+On Organization and Enterprise plans, check the administrator’s OAuth app allowlist if your coding client cannot connect to Figma. Ask the organization owner to approve the client through the normal process. Confirm which file and seat permissions are in effect. [Figma OAuth app controls](https://help.figma.com/hc/en-us/articles/44716871463319-Manage-OAuth-apps-and-MCP-clients-for-your-organization).
+
+Use the Dev Mode agent to inspect a design, compare versions, or request code and asset links. If you need editable native content, check whether the remote MCP client has a writing tool, a suitable seat, and permission to edit the destination. Verify the actual layers and relationships in that file. [Dev Mode release notes](https://www.figma.com/release-notes/) and [Figma MCP capabilities](https://developers.figma.com/docs/figma-mcp-server/).
+
 Use Figma plan features only when the chosen deliverable requires them. A variable-driven native prototype may have additional plan requirements. A Design review prototype should not inherit those requirements merely because the team’s foundations were created in Figma.
 
